Modifications made for Aegis Agent (starting 2026-09-28):

- Product renamed to Aegis Agent in the web interface, all translations, icons,
  tray, command line output, logs, default data and config directories, and
  packaging. Configuration environment variables (BACKREST_*) and internal Go
  package paths are unchanged.
- Documentation links point to the Aegis Agent repository; a command hook guide
  for Aegis Agent was added under docs/aegis.
- Reporting to Aegis Cloud (internal/aegis, new): one-way reports to the report
  URL set at install time. They hold finished operations (result, statistics,
  error messages, files that could not be read, the end of the operation log),
  running backups, the repositories and plans with their paths and schedules,
  and a heartbeat. Repository passwords, storage keys, restic command lines and
  snapshot contents are never sent. The connection state is served at
  /aegis/status and shown in the web interface header.
- Login is always required: the switch that turned authentication off was
  removed, and the server refuses a configuration that disables it.
- The web interface creates new repositories only on an Aegis Cloud storage,
  picked from the storages the agent was installed with; the storage key is
  read from the environment.
- Notification hooks other than commands are no longer offered for new hooks
  (alerts are sent by Aegis Cloud); existing hooks keep working.
- Multihost sync is turned off in the web interface.
- The restic binary shipped next to Aegis Agent is used before downloading one.
- Fix: a repository with backups but no check or prune yet no longer stops the
  agent from starting when the check or prune schedule is a cron expression
  counted from the last run (internal/protoutil/schedule.go).
- Packaging: releases are built by scripts/aegis-release.sh for Linux x86_64
  and arm64, with restic in the archive. install.sh was replaced by an
  installer for a root systemd service (/opt/aegis-agent, /etc/aegis-agent,
  /var/lib/aegis-agent) that checks downloads against SHA256SUMS. The Docker
  images are built from the binaries that script stages and carry the license
  texts in /licenses. Upstream's CI workflows, dependabot, funding and
  goreleaser configuration were removed; the issue templates name Aegis Agent.

Restic (https://restic.net), which Aegis Agent runs to perform backups, is
distributed under the BSD 2-Clause License. Its license text ships as
LICENSE.restic in the release archives and in /licenses of the Docker image.
The Docker image also contains Alpine Linux packages (tini, curl, bash, rclone,
openssh, tzdata, docker-cli), each under its own license.
